   "mydre",
   "About text",
   "myDRE is a Trusted Processing Environment run by anDREa B.V. on Microsoft Azure. An organisation takes a subscription and creates a workspace per research project; each workspace has its own storage and Windows or Linux virtual machines, on which researchers use the software they need (organisations can provide machine templates with, for example, Python, R and SPSS). Access is role-based and can include collaborators from other organisations, every action is logged, and data can only enter or leave a workspace through an approval step. Costs are the organisation's subscription plus pay-per-use Azure consumption. myDRE is used by [all] Dutch UMCs, for example to analyse sensitive health data or to run nodes for federated analysis."
